    "b-sks-rc-tl-intro": {
      "id": "b-sks-rc-tl-intro",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "TARGET LEDGER — Everything that has happened on a target. A target climbs through scored submissions; once it hits 100 % it is good. The agent reads the whole ledger before touching the target: every traced run, every imported PR, every exception. Three stored entry types feed it — "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker_run",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " (a traced engagement by a worker, with its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "submission",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows one per scored try and its integration outcome — "
        },
        {
          "insert": "integration",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "integration_detail",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — on the same row), "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pull_request",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " (an external PR that touched the target, reconstructed by the importer), and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "event",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " (the exception record: human "
        },
        {
          "insert": "note",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows; the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "regression",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " kind is defined but retired 2026-09-02, and nothing writes it). There is no shared parent table and no origin enum: each entry type is its own table, and the word \"attempt\" survives only as informal prose. Good news is never an event row: it is visible in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "target_status",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and in the runs and PRs themselves."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-sks-rc-tl-entry-types": {
      "id": "b-sks-rc-tl-entry-types",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Entry type",
          "What it records",
          "Written by",
          "Trace"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            [
              {
                "insert": "worker_run",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " + "
              },
              {
                "insert": "submission",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            "A harness worker's engagement with the target: goal, baseline, one row per scored try, final outcome, and the integration outcome (integrated or conflicted, with conflict paths)",
            "The worker summary agent, once at close; immutable",
            "Full: run-state artifacts, transcript, scored submissions"
          ],
          [
            [
              {
                "insert": "pull_request",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            "An external PR that touched the target: one deduced summary and an outcome, honestly labeled as reconstruction",
            "The PR importer; immutable",
            [
              {
                "insert": "None: no worker trace exists, so no "
              },
              {
                "insert": "submission",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " rows"
              }
            ]
          ],
          [
            [
              {
                "insert": "event",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " + "
              },
              {
                "insert": "event_ref",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "insert": "The exceptions: a human "
              },
              {
                "insert": "note",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": "; the "
              },
              {
                "insert": "regression",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " kind is retired (2026-09-02) and nothing writes it"
              }
            ],
            "A human (notes); append-only",
            [
              {
                "insert": "Refs: "
              },
              {
                "insert": "event_ref",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " rows name the worker run, epoch, PR, or commit involved"
              }
            ]
          ]
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-sks-rc-tl-view": {
      "id": "b-sks-rc-tl-view",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The ledger a worker reads is a derived view, never rows: the union of the three entry types for one target, chronological, newest first, conflicted runs highlighted with their conflict paths — "
        },
        {
          "insert": "submission",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows joined to their "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker_run",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows, merged with the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pull_request",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows and the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "event",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows. Nothing stores the union. The target card shows this view first, and it is where the card reads the target's latest activity — "
        },
        {
          "insert": "target_status",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " carries no last-run pointer. Per-run echo rows do not exist; the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "event",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " table holds only what the climb cannot tell on its own."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-sks-rc-tl-discord-note": {
      "id": "b-sks-rc-tl-discord-note",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Discord is never a ledger entry. Discord material enters the system only as facts and evidence on entities — mostly patterns and game concepts — via the importer; it never becomes a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker_run",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pull_request",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", or "
        },
        {
          "insert": "event",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-sks-rc-tl-split": {
      "id": "b-sks-rc-tl-split",
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "kind": "decision",
        "title": "Invariant — operational, not knowledge",
        "tone": "success"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Everything in this section is the operational world: what happened to the target, when, and how it scored. Storing a ledger entry does not make it knowledge. Becoming knowledge means the librarian writes a live "
        },
        {
          "insert": "fact",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row with a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "rationale",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and cited evidence — the fact's "
        },
        {
          "insert": "evidence",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows. Worker runs, submissions, and pull requests can be cited through "
        },
        {
          "insert": "attempt://",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pr://",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " locators but never speak as facts; an event is never cited directly — a citation points at the run, PR, or commit its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "event_ref",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows name."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
